  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "0xSero's DeepSeek V4 Flash REAP 162B (K144, 144 experts per layer, MXFP4, about 93.7 GB) on one Spark with vLLM, from 0xSero/deepseek-spark at 97fd6f02 (runtime/ configs and launcher; the vLLM Studio controller in the same repository is not packaged). Runs on upstream's public arm64 cutlass451-g27 vLLM image (pinned by digest) with upstream's GB10 REAP patcher applied at build time instead of at each start: router fallback for non-standard expert counts, per-layer MXFP4 memory hygiene, CUDA-IPC fix. 200000-token context, FP8 KV cache (fixed KV budget), one sequence, thinking on by default, DeepSeek V4 tokenizer, tool-call and reasoning parsers, CUDA graphs (FULL_AND_PIECEWISE), prefix caching. No speculative decoding (the k144-nospec-200k profile), larger KV budget and batch. Upstream publishes 200K-context sweeps for this profile in runtime/evidence; numbers are upstream claims and not repeated here. Licences are informational: weights repository and DeepSeek V4 are MIT; the source repository carries no licence file. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
